Historical definitions

Campaign settings 1 (in use when the snapshot was saved)

We are studying traffic safety in this area and want to hear from the people who travel here. Share the
specific places where walking, biking, driving, or reaching transit feels unsafe or uncomfortable, and what
you think would improve them. Your comments are reviewed by the project team and inform which
improvements are studied.

Categories

Crossing safety: Crosswalk visibility, crossing distance, signal timing, turning conflicts, and near-miss
locations.

Sidewalks and accessibility: Sidewalk gaps, narrow walkways, ADA barriers, surface conditions, and curb
ramp issues.

Bicycle comfort and network gaps: Bicycle stress points, missing links, uncomfortable crossings, and route
continuity concerns.

Transit access and stops: Stop placement, stop amenities, crossings to stops, and first/last-mile access.

Driver behavior and speed: Speeding, red-light and stop-sign running, aggressive turning, and passing too
close.

Maintenance, lighting, and visibility: Vegetation, pavement, drainage, lighting, signage, striping, and sight-line
maintenance issues.

Other / needs follow-up: Useful comments that are still too broad, mixed, or ambiguous for a tighter category
assignment.

Questions

Retained translations

No translations in this definition.



